IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc97-nouns`

-- MAGNA CARTA (1297), LAYER 1: CHAPTER 9, "Liberties of London, &c."
-- Source: aep-Edw1cc1929-25-9-extract.md, the heading (line 31) and the text of chapter IX (line 32).
-- Two sentences. The first gives the City of London all the old Liberties and Customs [which it hath been used to have].
-- The second gives every other City, Borough, Town, and the Barons of the Five Ports and all other Ports their Liberties
-- and free Customs. The bracketed words are the traditional translation's insertion; this encoding takes the text as given.
-- Nothing here says the chapter is, or ever was, in force.
--
-- The text names no one who must give effect to these entitlements. "We will and grant" names the granter; "shall have"
-- creates no duty on anyone the text names. So the rules here are decisions about what a community shall have, not
-- regulative rules (see the Jural relations table in NOTES.md and the fork register, F-C9-DUTY).

§ `Chapter 9: Liberties of London, &c.`

§§ `The first sentence: the City of London`

-- gloss (not the text's): "old" and "hath been used to have" are not defined; the asker states both as facts.
-- With the bracket, both are needed. Without it (F-C9-BRACKET) only "old" would be.
-- src:32 | THE City of London shall have all the old Liberties and Customs [which it hath been used to have].
@ref Magna Carta (1297), chapter 9, first sentence (src:32)
GIVEN community IS A Community
      `the Liberty or Custom is old` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the City hath been used to have it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Coverage
`chapter 9, first sentence: the City of London shall have` community `the Liberty or Custom is old` `the City hath been used to have it` MEANS
    IF      community EQUALS `the City of London`
        AND `the Liberty or Custom is old`
        AND `the City hath been used to have it`
    THEN `covered by the text`
    -- not covered, silent: the first sentence is about the City of London; and "old" and "hath been used to have" are undefined, so the asker states them.
    ELSE `not covered by the text`

§§ `The second sentence: the other Cities, Boroughs, Towns and Ports`

-- gloss (not the text's): "free" is read as qualifying "Customs" only, as the words are printed ("their Liberties and free
-- Customs"); the asker says whether a Custom is free. See F-C9-FREE. "their" is the community's own: the asker says whether the
-- Liberty or Custom is the community's own (fork F-C9-THEIR).
-- src:32 | Moreover We will and grant, that all other Cities, Boroughs, Towns, and the Barons of the Five Ports, and all other Ports, shall have all their Liberties and free Customs.
@ref Magna Carta (1297), chapter 9, second sentence (src:32)
GIVEN community IS A Community
      thing IS A `Liberty or Custom`
      `it is the community's own` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Custom is free` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Coverage
`chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` community thing `it is the community's own` `the Custom is free` MEANS
    IF `it is the community's own`
    THEN
        IF      community EQUALS `another City`
             OR community EQUALS `a Borough`
             OR community EQUALS `a Town`
             OR community EQUALS `a Baron of the Five Ports`
             OR community EQUALS `another Port`
        THEN
            CONSIDER thing
                WHEN `a Liberty` THEN `covered by the text`
                WHEN `a Custom` THEN
                    IF `the Custom is free`
                    THEN `covered by the text`
                    -- not covered, silent: the sentence names "free Customs" and does not say whether a Custom that is not free is excluded.
                    ELSE `not covered by the text`
        -- not covered, unclosed list: the communities are listed, not closed with "only"; a community of another kind is not addressed.
        ELSE `not covered by the text`
    -- not covered, silent: "their" is the community's own (F-C9-THEIR); a Liberty or Custom that is not its own is not addressed.
    ELSE `not covered by the text`

§§ `Both sentences: what the community shall have, in the text's words`

-- The text's own words for what each community shall have; a community the chapter does not name gets "not covered".
@ref Magna Carta (1297), chapter 9, both sentences (src:32)
GIVEN community IS A Community
GIVETH A `Chapter 9 entitlement`
`chapter 9: what the community shall have` community MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF community EQUALS `the City of London`
        THEN `all the old Liberties and Customs which it hath been used to have`
        IF      community EQUALS `another City`
             OR community EQUALS `a Borough`
             OR community EQUALS `a Town`
             OR community EQUALS `a Baron of the Five Ports`
             OR community EQUALS `another Port`
        THEN `all their Liberties and free Customs`
        -- not covered, unclosed list: the communities are listed, not closed with "only"; a community of another kind is not addressed.
        OTHERWISE `not covered by chapter 9`

-- The one question both sentences answer together: does the community keep this Liberty or Custom?
-- For the City of London the first sentence governs (the kind of thing and "free" do not matter);
-- for the others the second sentence governs. A community of another kind is not covered by either.
@ref Magna Carta (1297), chapter 9, both sentences (src:32)
GIVEN community IS A Community
      thing IS A `Liberty or Custom`
      `the Liberty or Custom is old` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the community hath been used to have it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the community's own` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Custom is free` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Coverage
`chapter 9: the community keeps the Liberty or Custom` community thing `the Liberty or Custom is old` `the community hath been used to have it` `it is the community's own` `the Custom is free` MEANS
    IF community EQUALS `the City of London`
    THEN `chapter 9, first sentence: the City of London shall have` community `the Liberty or Custom is old` `the community hath been used to have it`
    ELSE `chapter 9, second sentence: the other communities shall have` community thing `it is the community's own` `the Custom is free`

-- "shall have" is in the passive in both sentences: the text names no one who must give effect to the entitlements ("We will and
-- grant" names the granter, which is not the same), and none is invented. The answer is NOTHING, whoever asks (fork F-C9-DUTY).
-- src:32 | THE City of London shall have all the old Liberties and Customs [which it hath been used to have].
-- src:32 | that all other Cities, Boroughs, Towns, and the Barons of the Five Ports, and all other Ports, shall have all their Liberties and free Customs.
@ref Magna Carta (1297), chapter 9, who is to give effect (src:32)
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`chapter 9: the party the text names to give effect to the entitlements` MEANS NOTHING
